  "final_message": "I put `channel` back, so CI should pass. I couldn't run `arch` or the ARCH-4 contract check here. Typecheck passes and all 39 tests pass.\n\nThe check that failed is not in this repo. It shows `analytics-ingest` still requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`). So the premise that nothing reads `channel` was wrong, and I should have checked consumers before removing it. `billing-service` was unaffected.\n\nI reverted the whole removal, not just the event field. The event takes its value from the order, so the field had to come back in the model and the `POST /orders` input as well. The code, tests, `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md` example now match the original behavior, and `schemaVersion` is still 3.\n\nThe working tree is currently uncommitted changes on top of the commit that removed the field. I haven't committed anything.\n\nIf you still want `channel` gone, the consumer has to change first. `analytics-ingest` would need to stop requiring it, or the field would need a deprecation window with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can redo the removal once that's done.",
